A||||3||hugh||Where is fan relay on 88GT||||1||
Z||000000||hugh||08-06-2000||07:21 PM||||I have had an 88 GT for about 3 months.The digital gauges were very erratic.For the first time today I had a chance to check it.Whoever put the gauges in didn't properly connect the positive,negative or sensor wires.Now the wires are properly done there is feedback from the radiator fan,and when I turn off the ignition the voltage generated by the fan keeps the engine running until the voltage gets too low to maintain the ignition.I want to use a relay to keep the fan supply isolated.Even if I have to use a relay to control a relay.   I've already used the search function,there are no relays near the left headlight.There 2 relays in the trunk at the firewall. <p>[This message has been edited by hugh (edited 08-06-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000001||Indiana_resto_guy||08-06-2000||09:55 PM||||The fan relay should be located in the head light bucket in front of the assembly. It looks like an oval box about 1 inch across, lugs in at the bottom and is held on by two screws on top.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Indiana_resto_guy||08-06-2000||09:55 PM||||The fan relay should be located in the head light bucket in front of the assembly. It looks like an oval box about 1 inch across, lugs in at the bottom and is held on by two screws on top.||||reg||1
Z||000003||hugh||08-07-2000||09:42 PM||||I couldn't find the relay,because it wasn't there.Someone removed the relay and connected the coil wire (of the relay) to the fan wire.DUMB!!! I cut the wires off the base and wired in a Bosch relay.Right now I have the control wire grounded so the fan will run whenever the switch is on.I'll wire in a thermostat later.Thanks for the help.||||reg||1
